# Affine Repository Directory Structure

This document outlines the perceived directory structure of the Affine repository, based on the provided file summaries. The repository appears to be a monorepo, organizing various components and applications under distinct top-level directories.

## Top-Level Structure

The repository is primarily structured into three main directories: `blocksuite`, `packages`, and `tools`.

### `blocksuite`

This directory seems to contain core building blocks, foundational UI components, or a low-level framework layer for the application. It likely houses common UI elements, block models, rendering utilities, and data structures that are fundamental to how content is represented and interacted with in Affine.

-   **`blocksuite/affine/blocks/`**: Contains definitions and components for various block types (e.g., `bookmark-block.ts` for bookmark blocks, `divider-model.ts` for divider blocks). This suggests a modular approach to content elements.
-   **`blocksuite/affine/components/`**: Houses shared UI components used across the block suite (e.g., `color-picker/types.ts`, `toolbar/icon-button.ts`).
-   **`blocksuite/affine/data-view/`**: Appears to relate to data visualization and presentation, including expression, grouping, and logical typing (`expression/types.ts`, `group-by/types.ts`, `logical/type.ts`).
-   **`blocksuite/affine/ext-loader/`**: Implies an extension loading mechanism for adding functionality to the block suite (`store-provider.ts`, `view-provider.ts` defining `StoreExtensionContext`, `ViewExtensionContext`).
-   **`blocksuite/affine/gfx/`**: Contains graphics-related utilities and types, possibly for rendering blocks (e.g., `turbo-renderer/src/types.ts` defining `BlockLayout`).
-   **`blocksuite/affine/model/`**: Defines data models and constants specific to the block suite, such as block properties, text styles, and mindmap layouts (`consts/mindmap.ts`, `consts/text.ts`, `themes/color.ts`, `blocks/divider/divider-model.ts`).
-   **`blocksuite/affine/shared/`**: Contains shared adapters and utilities that are crucial for integrating different content formats or services with the block suite (`adapters/html/block-adapter.ts`, `adapters/markdown/block-adapter.ts`, `services/telemetry-service/types.ts`, `utils/signal.ts`).
-   **`blocksuite/framework/global/`**: Likely the global framework utilities and core services like dependency injection (`di/`), error handling (`exceptions/`), and graphics primitives (`gfx/`).
-   **`blocksuite/framework/std/`**: Standard library or common utilities within the framework, including event handling, graphics models, and scope management (`event/state/pointer.ts`, `gfx/model/model.ts`, `scope/std-scope.ts`).
-   **`blocksuite/framework/store/`**: Deals with the application's data store, including block models, reactive text, schema validation, and transformers (`model/block/block-model.ts`, `reactive/text/types.ts`, `schema/error.ts`, `transformer/type.ts`).

### `packages`

This is a significant part of the monorepo, holding distinct, reusable modules, libraries, or applications.

#### `packages/backend`

Contains backend-specific code, likely for server-side functionalities.

-   **`packages/backend/server/src/mails/components/workspace.tsx`**: Suggests email templates or components related to workspace notifications, possibly using React for server-side rendering.
-   **`packages/backend/server/src/models/common/`**: Defines common data models used by the backend (`doc.ts`, `role.ts` for `WorkspaceRole`).
-   **`packages/backend/server/src/plugins/payment/types.ts`**: Indicates payment processing related types and logic (`SubscriptionRecurring`).

#### `packages/common`

This prefix signifies common utilities or infrastructure used across different parts of the application, often shared between frontend and backend.

-   **`packages/common/debug/src/index.ts`**: Provides a `DebugLogger` class for centralized logging.
-   **`packages/common/env/src/`**: Manages environment-related constants and configurations (`constant.ts` defining `Unreachable` error, `workspace/legacy-cloud/index.ts` for workspace permissions).
-   **`packages/common/graphql/src/schema.ts`**: Defines shared GraphQL interfaces and enums (`Mutation`, `SubscriptionRecurring`), indicating the application interacts with a GraphQL API.
-   **`packages/common/infra/src/framework/`**: Contains core infrastructure components, possibly a different framework layer than `blocksuite/framework`. This includes dependency injection (`core/framework.ts`, `core/provider.ts`, `core/types.ts`) and reactive data streams (`livedata/livedata.ts`).
-   **`packages/common/nbstore/src/connection/connection.ts`**: Defines types for connection status, likely for real-time data or synchronization.
-   **`packages/common/y-octo/core/src/`**: Appears to be a core data synchronization or CRDT (Conflict-free Replicated Data Type) library, possibly written in Rust (indicated by `.rs` files).
    -   **`packages/common/y-octo/core/src/doc/`**: Handles document structure, codecs, and types (`codec/any.rs`, `codec/io/codec_v1.rs`, `document.rs`, `types/value.rs`).
-   **`packages/common/y-octo/node/src/text.rs`**: Node.js bindings for the Y-Octo text type.

#### `packages/frontend`

This directory contains client-side application code, potentially for various platforms.

-   **`packages/frontend/apps/android/`**: Android application code, specifically `app/src/main/java/app/affine/pro/service/SSEService.kt` suggests Server-Sent Events (SSE) handling in Kotlin.
-   **`packages/frontend/apps/ios/`**: iOS application code. This is a prominent part of the structure.
    -   **`packages/frontend/apps/ios/App/Packages/AffineGraphQL/`**: A dedicated Swift package for handling GraphQL operations in the iOS application, including generated schema definitions and query files (`Sources/Schema/`, `Sources/Operations/Queries/`).
    -   **`packages/frontend/apps/ios/App/Packages/Intelligents/`**: Suggests components related to "Intelligents" features, possibly AI or smart functionalities within the iOS app (`Sources/Intelligents/Interface/View/ChatList/ChatListItem.swift`).
-   **`packages/frontend/component/src/`**: Reusable frontend UI components (`lit-react/create-component.ts`, `ui/radio/types.ts`).
-   **`packages/frontend/core/src/`**: The main core frontend logic, likely shared across different frontend applications (web, desktop, mobile).
    -   **`packages/frontend/core/src/blocksuite/ai/`**: Components related to AI features integrated with the block suite (`ai-chat-chips/type.ts`, `ai-chat-messages/type.ts`, `peek-view/date-time.ts`).
    -   **`packages/frontend/core/src/components/explorer/docs-view/doc-list-item.tsx`**: UI components for document listings in an explorer view.
    -   **`packages/frontend/core/src/desktop/`**: Desktop-specific components, particularly for dialogs and settings (`dialogs/setting/account-setting/storage-progress.tsx`, `dialogs/setting/general-setting/plans/cloud-plans.tsx`).
    -   **`packages/frontend/core/src/mobile/`**: Mobile-specific components (`components/rename/type.ts`).
    -   **`packages/frontend/core/src/modules/`**: Contains modularized application logic, services, and entities.
        -   **`packages/frontend/core/src/modules/collection-rules/types.ts`**: Defines types for filtering, grouping, and ordering data collections.
        -   **`packages/frontend/core/src/modules/doc/services/docs.ts`**: Service for managing documents.
        -   **`packages/frontend/core/src/modules/editor-setting/schema.ts`**: Editor settings schema (`FontFamily`).
        -   **`packages/frontend/core/src/modules/pdf/renderer/types.ts`**: PDF rendering types.
        -   **`packages/frontend/core/src/modules/workbench/`**: Logic and components related to the main workbench/editor area (`entities/view.ts`, `scopes/view.ts`, `view/sidebar/sidebar-header.tsx`).
        -   **`packages/frontend/core/src/modules/workspace/`**: Core logic for workspace management, including metadata, open options, and various services (`metadata.ts`, `open-options.ts`, `services/flavours.ts`, `services/list.ts`, `services/profile.ts`).
-   **`packages/frontend/i18n/src/i18n.gen.ts`**: Generated internationalization (i18n) strings and hooks.

### `tests`

Contains end-to-end (e2e) tests for the block suite.

-   **`tests/blocksuite/e2e/utils/actions/edgeless.ts`**: Utilities for simulating user actions in "edgeless" mode (likely a whiteboard or freeform canvas).

### `tools`

This directory typically houses development, build, or utility scripts that support the project but are not part of the main application logic.

-   **`tools/@types/env/__all.d.ts`**: Global type definitions for environment variables.
-   **`tools/utils/src/logger.ts`**: A utility for logging within the tooling itself.
-   **`tools/utils/src/workspace.ts`**: Utilities for understanding and interacting with the monorepo's package structure, including package names and access to package-specific functionalities.

This comprehensive structure suggests a complex application that supports multiple platforms (web, desktop, iOS, Android), heavily relies on a component-based architecture, utilizes GraphQL for data fetching, and incorporates sophisticated data synchronization (CRDTs). The `blocksuite` acts as a powerful content engine, while `packages/frontend/core` provides the overarching application logic for the user interface.
